course: dictionary
lesson: 10380
title: A word from history: trebuchet
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A trebuchet is a word you may meet in a history book or a science lesson. You do not need to know it before you start. Use the words around it to work out what it means. «Attackers besieged castles with catapults and trebuchets, or tried to starve the defenders out.»
explain: The clues are besieged, castles, starve and defenders. Besieged means attackers surround a place for a long time. Starving the defenders out means waiting until the people inside run out of food. So a trebuchet must be something used in war against castles. Trebuchets were not castles or people. They were weapons.
explain: Now test your idea by swapping it into the sentence: «Attackers besieged castles with a huge machine that throws stones.» It still makes sense, so your meaning fits. A trebuchet is a machine, and you can picture it throwing stones at a castle wall.
fact: A trebuchet is a huge medieval siege machine, like a giant catapult, that throws heavy stones over castle walls.
fact: A trebuchet is powered by a heavy counterweight that falls and swings a long arm with a sling on the end.
fact: In 1304, Edward I used a huge trebuchet called «Warwolf» at Stirling Castle.
fact: Cannons from the 1400s made castle walls far less useful, so trebuchets were no longer the main weapon against castles.
fact: In science and design and technology lessons, pupils build small model trebuchets to learn about levers, forces and energy.
exercise: «Attackers besieged castles for weeks or months with catapults and trebuchets.» What is a trebuchet? | *A huge medieval machine that throws heavy stones over castle walls | A soft kind of castle wall | A type of cannon from the 1400s | A stone bridge over a river
exercise: What powers a trebuchet? | Batteries that need charging | The wind blowing through the castle | Steam from a kettle | *A heavy counterweight that falls and swings the arm
exercise: Pupils build a model trebuchet in science. What might they learn about? | The names of kings only | How to paint a castle | How to bake bread | *Levers, forces and energy
test: In «Attackers besieged castles with catapults and trebuchets», which word helps you know a trebuchet was used as a weapon? | *Catapults, which are weapons too | Attackers, who are people | Castles, which are built of stone | Besieged, which is a long word
test: According to the text, what made castle walls far less useful from the 1400s? | Gardens | Rain | *Cannons | Carpets
exam: In «Attackers besieged castles with catapults and trebuchets», what is the best clue that a trebuchet is a weapon? | Attackers, who are people | Castles, which are built of stone | The word with, which is a small word | *Catapults, which are weapons like it
